# Line endings (2026-09-15).
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but every shell
# script, Dockerfile and compose file it produces RUNS ON LINUX, on the EC2
# box. A .sh file checked out with CRLF fails there immediately and
# confusingly:
#
#   ./build-frontends.sh: /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# So: normalise text to LF in the repository, and force LF on checkout for
# everything that Linux executes or parses. Windows editors handle LF fine;
# Linux does not handle CRLF.

# Default: let git normalise text files to LF in the object store.
* text=auto

# Executed or parsed on Linux - must be LF on disk, on every platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.env.example   text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf

# Lua scripts are read by Redis at runtime from inside the image.
*.lua           text eol=lf

# SQL migrations are applied by the migrate role on Linux.
*.sql           text eol=lf

# Binary - never touch.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.pdf           binary
